---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

// FINAL source: cueory-privacy-p4.md, adopted 2026-11-17 (full SHA-256
// 02b71d707ee723f0a7e4f9922cb9af015a9d4f5b518c445a006f8e4353f2574f). Word for word; change it only with
// Christian's approval.
const email = site.contactEmail;
const mail = `mailto:${email}`;
---

<Layout title="privacy" description="What Cueory stores, what it doesn't, and how to delete or export your data.">
  <Prose>
    <h1>privacy, in plain language</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">Effective 19 November 2026</p>

    <p>
      Cueory is a free study site for nursing students, run by an individual in Arizona, USA. Public accounts are closed.
      You can study and play without giving us your email address. Your browser keeps your study progress and game
      results on your device. If you join the email list, send feedback or leave a tip, the information involved is
      described below.
    </p>

    <h2>Studying on this device</h2>
    <p>
      If you enter your course or exam date, star a card, or sort cards into “know it” and “still learning,” your browser
      saves those choices on this device. You can view, download or forget them on
      <a href="/progress">your progress page</a>. A study activity can also remember its page, question, timer and your
      answers so far. That saved place expires after 14 days. Clearing Cueory’s site data in your browser removes these
      records.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your browser may keep copies of the homepage, lessons you visit and site files so that you can reopen them offline.
      These copies contain the page content. Your answers and progress are stored separately. Cueory’s offline cache
      excludes daily games.
    </p>

    <h2>Playing daily games</h2>
    <p>
      If your browser allows storage, it automatically saves finished games on this device. Playing a game does not send
      your score to Cueory. For each result the browser can remember the puzzle date, whether you solved it, how many
      tries it took and whether you finished on a later day. Crossword results can record whether a solve counts toward a
      streak. Word path can also record how many cues you used and whether you found the special answer first. For
      sudoku, the browser saves the level, date and time taken for your first solve of each level each day. The games use
      these records to show results, times and streaks.
    </p>
    <p>
      piccline also saves the board you are playing today on this device: which answers you have found, the other
      words you found, the cues you used and how many words did not count. That lets a reload bring the board back, and a finished board
      stays finished that day. It holds one day only and starts over the next day. It is never sent to Cueory.
    </p>
    <p>
      Opening <a href="/play">Daily Games</a> or a pillo, crossword, sudoku or word path page deletes general results
      and sudoku solve times older than 400 days. When your browser blocks storage, it cannot keep your results.
    </p>
    <p>
      On Daily Games, “forget” deletes that game’s saved results; for sudoku this includes its per-level times. “Forget
      all my stats” deletes every game’s results and sudoku’s times, and stays available while any are saved. If your
      browser refuses a deletion, the stats panel keeps the results and “forget” buttons for anything still stored.
      Clearing Cueory’s site data in your browser also removes these records, along with your other Cueory settings. If
      you finish another game afterward, your browser starts saving results again.
    </p>

    <h2>Settings and reminders</h2>
    <p>
      Your browser can remember whether you chose the light or dark theme, your game settings such as sound, contrast,
      timer and motion, and which games’ instructions you have seen. To decide when to suggest adding Cueory to your home
      screen, it can remember up to three dates on which you finished a puzzle and whether you dismissed that suggestion.
    </p>
    <p>
      There are two reminders about the email list. Your browser saves when the launch-list panel appeared so it can stay
      out of the way for 30 days. On eligible pages, a separate signup pop-up may appear after 10 seconds of viewing. The
      browser saves the time under <code>cueory-signup-popup-seen</code> when it shows the pop-up and updates the time
      when you close it, follow its link or leave the page while it is open. It uses that time to keep the pop-up away for three hours.
      Lessons and game boards do not show the pop-up. Seeing a reminder does not subscribe you. Clearing Cueory’s site
      data removes both reminder records.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some features are still being built. Where enabled, glove notes remember which notes appeared in this tab, when the
      visit started, when the last message glove appeared and which gloves were used, the last welcome note on this
      device and your note-sound choice. The break timer can remember its state in this tab for up to two hours. A survey prompt can remember that you dismissed it. The dismissal record contains no survey answers.
    </p>

    <h2>Joining the launch email list</h2>
    <p>
      The “get launch updates” email box (on the home page and in the signup pop-up) sends the email address you type
      straight to Kit; Cueory’s own servers never receive it. Kit can also be reached through Cueory’s signup page on Kit.
      If you subscribe, you give your email address to Kit, which manages the list and sends Cueory’s updates and study
      tips for us. Joining the list does not create a
      Cueory account. Use the unsubscribe link in an email to stop receiving updates, or contact us about your
      subscription. Clearing browser data leaves your subscription in place.
      <a href="https://cueory.kit.com/bfd9609b46" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kit signup page</a> ·
      <a href="https://kit.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kit privacy policy</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Contacting Cueory</h2>
    <p>
      When you email us, we receive your email address, the name your email service shows, your message and anything you
      attach. We use those details to respond, handle requests and correct reported errors. Please keep patient
      information, confidential exam material and other people’s private information out of your messages. If you
      accidentally send patient information, follow your school’s or facility’s reporting procedure and start a new
      message telling us approximately when and where you sent it. Leave out the patient details and the original
      message. <a href={mail}>Email Cueory</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Tips, videos and social links</h2>
    <p>
      Tips are optional. Ko-fi requires users to be at least 18. The payment is handled through Ko-fi by PayPal or
      Stripe. As the recipient, Cueory may see your supporter name, email address, payment amount and any message you
      choose to send. Depending on the settings you choose, a Ko-fi message may be public. We use payment details to
      manage tips, answer refund questions and keep records where required. A tip does not change your access to the
      site. For a mistaken payment, email us and leave out card or bank details.
      <a href="https://more.ko-fi.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ko-fi privacy policy</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      If a lesson offers a video, its YouTube player loads only when you choose to play it. YouTube may then receive your
      connection details, record the play or set cookies. If you follow a social link, the destination receives your
      visit under its own privacy policy.
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google privacy policy</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and visit statistics</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare delivers Cueory’s pages. It processes connection details such as your IP address and browser
      information to deliver and protect the site. Cueory uses Cloudflare Web Analytics to see page-visit and performance
      statistics. That analytics service does not use cookies or build a profile to follow you across sites. Cueory does
      not sell personal information or show ads on its own pages. Cueory does not track you across other websites, so it
      does not respond differently to Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signals. Other services you choose to use
      from Cueory, such as YouTube, Kit or Ko-fi, may collect information about your activity over time and across sites
      under their own policies.
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Children’s information</h2>
    <p>
      Cueory and its launch email list are for people aged 16 and over. We do not knowingly collect personal information
      from children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 gave us personal information, a parent or guardian can
      email <a href={mail}>{email}</a>. Please leave sensitive information out of the first message. If we learn we
      collected a child’s personal information, we will promptly delete it from our records and ask any provider holding
      it for us to do the same, except where the law requires us to keep it.
    </p>

    <h2>Your information and questions</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={mail}>{email}</a> to ask what personal information we hold about you or to request a copy,
      correction or deletion. We may need to confirm that the information is yours. We can handle records we control and
      ask a provider to help where it acts for us. Your browser’s local study and game records can be cleared on the
      device where you used Cueory. For records held independently by a payment provider or social platform, use that
      service’s privacy controls.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we change how Cueory handles personal information, we’ll update this notice and its date.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a> · <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>
